columns_may_be_interleaved:no_enacting_or_operative_words)"},{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"provisional NO, but no job found a whole-order-end candidate"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:11568\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-11-18/pdf/FR-1970-11-18.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 66437513e79ee3047d2b3a30143146a4fdcfaaa8da66645182fc504ab54ccef3\nLocation: 35 FR 17703, PDF pages 9-9 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 9 of 80 ===\nTHE PRESIDENT 17703\nExecutive Order 1 1 5 6 8\nEXEMPTING A. EVERETTE MadNTYRE FROM COMPULSORY  \nRETIREMENT FOR AGE\nW HEREAS A. Everette MacIntyre, a member of the Federal \nTrade Commission, will, during the month of February 1971, become \nsubject to compulsory retirement for age under the provisions of \nsection 8335 of title 5, United States Code, unless exempted therefrom \nby Executive order; and\nW HEREAS, in my judgment, the public interest requires that \nMr. MacIntyre be exempted from such compulsory retirement:\nNOW, TH EREFORE, by virtue of the authority vested in me \nby subsection (c) of section 8335 of title 5, United States Code, I  here­\nby exempt A. Everette MacIntyre from compulsory retirement for \nage until February 29,1972.\nT h e W h ite H ouse,\nNovember 16,1970.\n[F.R. Doc. 70-15586; Filed, Nov. 16, 1970; 1:00 p.m.]\nFEDERAL REGISTER, V O L  35, NO. 224— WEDNESDAY, NOVEMBER 18, 1970\n","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_11568.txt","sha256":"3eb807f08aff152d158ad9fbc47614335de80724f1ab085642b4c18d9cfeaeed","source":{"line":1335,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"872d823a3d63161d869656c1ff140b1e0e5e160452eeeb8ec25a7dcff77b517d"}}]}
